// Bug 21: a `[:` without a closing `:]` in a polymorphic FFI texture's body
// is dropped. `monomorphize` (CompilePolymorphicFFI.cpp) takes `[:` for the
// start of a `[:Name:]` placeholder and, when the body ends before `:]`,
// writes only the text after it: the byte string below reaches rustc as
// b"ab". (lean2rr's string literal table is such a body: a Lean literal
// "a[:3]" printed as "a3]".)
// Expected: prints 4. Reussir ef922049: prints 2.
#[ffi(import)]
fn say(x : u64) [{ println!("{}", x) }];
#[ffi(import)]
fn unterminated_len() -> u64 [{ b"a[:b".len() as u64 }];
#[main]
fn main() { say(unterminated_len()); }
